Project Demonstration Phase
Legalease – Project Demonstration Phase

The Project Demonstration Phase is the stage where the developed Legalease system is presented to users, teachers, evaluators, or project guides to show how the proposed system works in practice.

1. Introduction

Legalease is a smart legal information platform that helps users understand basic legal information in simple language. During the demonstration, the major features, user interface, workflow, and expected outputs of the system are shown.

2. Demonstration Objectives

The demonstration aims to:

Show the working of the Legalease application.
Explain the major modules and features.
Demonstrate how a user interacts with the system.
Show how legal questions are processed.
Demonstrate document/template generation.
Show links to relevant official legal resources.
Explain the benefits and limitations of the system.
3. Demonstration Flow
Step 1 – User Registration/Login

The user opens Legalease and creates an account or logs into an existing account.

Login / Register
       ↓
Legalease Dashboard
Step 2 – Enter a Legal Query

The user enters a question in simple language.

Example:

“I purchased a product online, but the seller has not delivered it. What can I do?”

Step 3 – Query Processing

The system analyzes the user's question using NLP/AI and identifies the relevant category.

User Question
      ↓
Natural Language Processing
      ↓
Legal Category Identification
      ↓
Relevant Information Retrieval
Step 4 – Display Information

The system provides a simple explanation of the relevant legal topic and possible general steps the user may consider.

The system should clearly indicate that the information is general information and not a substitute for professional legal advice.

Step 5 – Official Resources

The application provides links to appropriate official government/legal resources where the user can obtain further information or submit a complaint.

Step 6 – Document Generation

If appropriate, the user can select a document template.

For example:

Select Document
      ↓
Enter Required Details
      ↓
Generate Document
      ↓
Preview / Download
